1
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:22,800
Dark and difficult times lie ahead.

2
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:39,600
Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire is a adventure,
fantasy film directed by Mike Newell.

3
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:56,400
When Harry Potter's name emerges from the Goblet of Fire, he becomes a competitor in a
grueling battle for glory among three wizarding schools—the Triwizard Tournament.

4
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:13,200
But since Harry never submitted his name for the Tournament, who did?

5
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:30,000
Now Harry must confront a deadly dragon, fierce water demons and an enchanted maze
only to find himself in the cruel grasp of He Who Must Not Be Named.

6
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:46,800
Harry Potter, played by Daniel Radcliffe.

7
00:43:57,599 --> 00:44:03,599
Ron Weasley, played by Rupert Grint.

8
00:50:14,400 --> 00:50:20,400
Hermione Granger, played by Emma Watson.

9
00:56:31,200 --> 00:56:37,200
Alastor 'Mad-Eye' Moody, played by Brendan Gleeson.

10
01:02:48,000 --> 01:02:54,000
Albus Dumbledore, played by Michael Gambon.

11
01:09:04,800 --> 01:09:10,800
Cedric Diggory, played by Robert Pattinson.

12
01:15:21,600 --> 01:15:27,600
Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire is a 2005 fantasy film directed
by Mike Newell from a screenplay by Steve Kloves.

13
01:21:38,400 --> 01:21:44,400
It is based on the 2000 novel Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire by J.

14
01:27:55,199 --> 01:28:01,199
It is the sequel to Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban (2004) and
the fourth instalment in the Harry Potter film series.

15
01:34:12,000 --> 01:34:18,000
The film stars Daniel Radcliffe as Harry Potter, alongside Rupert Grint and Emma Watson
as Harry's best friends Ron Weasley and Hermione Granger, respectively.

16
01:40:28,800 --> 01:40:34,800
The story follows Harry's fourth year at Hogwarts, as he is chosen by the
Goblet of Fire to compete in the Triwizard Tournament.

17
01:46:45,600 --> 01:46:51,600
Principal photography began in early 2004, and the film
premiered worldwide on 18 November 2005.

18
01:53:02,400 --> 01:53:08,400
Five days following release, it had earned over US$102 million at the North American box office, the third-highest
first-weekend tally for a Harry Potter film behind Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows – Part 1 and Part 2.

19
01:59:19,199 --> 01:59:25,199
Goblet of Fire enjoyed a successful run at the box office, grossing $896 million worldwide and becoming
the highest-grossing film of 2005 and the sixth-highest-grossing film in the series.

20
02:05:36,000 --> 02:05:42,000
The film was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Art Direction
and won the BAFTA Award for Best Production Design.

21
02:11:52,800 --> 02:11:58,800
Goblet of Fire was the second film in the series to be released in IMAX.

22
02:18:09,600 --> 02:18:15,600
The film received positive reviews.

23
02:24:26,399 --> 02:24:32,399
It was followed by Harry Potter and the Order of the Phoenix in 2007.

24
02:30:43,200 --> 02:30:49,200
The film explores themes of witch, dying and death, based
on novel or book, magic, boarding school.
